## 3. User Flow

**New Visitor to Dashboard**

1.  A user visits the homepage (`/`). They see a clean landing page with a header, a dark mode toggle, and links to "Sign Up" and "Log In."
2.  They click "Sign Up," fill in email and password, and submit. The form calls the Better Auth API route. On success, the user is redirected to `/dashboard`.

**Returning User Experience**

1.  A returning user selects "Log In," enters credentials, and is authenticated via the same API route.
2.  After login, they arrive at `/dashboard`: a layout with a left sidebar (links to Dashboard, Profile, Settings) and a main area showing a welcome message, recent activity, and placeholder cards.
3.  The user can toggle dark/light mode at any time; their preference is saved and applied on subsequent visits.

## 4. Core Features

*   **User Authentication**\
    • Secure registration, login, logout, session handling (Better Auth).\
    • API routes under `/app/api/auth/[...all]/route.ts`.
*   **Database Integration**\
    • Drizzle ORM + PostgreSQL.\
    • Pre-configured `auth` schema in `/db/schema/auth.ts`.
*   **UI Component Library**\
    • Unstyled primitives from shadcn/ui in `/components/ui`.\
    • Utility classes via Tailwind CSS v4.
*   **Dark Mode & Theming**\
    • Theme toggle component, context hook, and cookie persistence.
*   **Routing & Layouts**\
    • Next.js App Router with nested layouts: global (`/app/layout.tsx`), dashboard (`/app/dashboard/layout.tsx`).
*   **One-Command Docker Setup**\
    • `docker-compose.yml` for Next.js server and Postgres instance.\
    • `.env.example` for required environment variables.
*   **Feature Blueprint**\
    • Example `/app/dashboard/` directory to guide adding new sections (e.g., `/app/dashboard/products`).

