## 6. Non-Functional Requirements

*   **Performance**:\
    • Cold start of app < 2 seconds.\
    • API response times < 200 ms under average load.
*   **Security**:\
    • HTTPS assumed in production.\
    • Passwords hashed by Better Auth.\
    • Environment variables not checked into Git.
*   **Usability**:\
    • Responsive UI (mobile to desktop).\
    • Accessible components (ARIA attributes, keyboard navigation).
*   **Scalability**:\
    • Modular folder structure to add new features without conflict.\
    • TypeScript types across server/client for safer refactors.

## 7. Constraints & Assumptions

*   **Environment**: Docker and Docker Compose must be installed locally.
*   **Dependencies**: Better Auth, Drizzle ORM, shadcn/ui must remain compatible with Next.js version.
*   **Assumptions**:\
    • Developers are familiar with Git, Node.js, and basic Docker commands.\
    • PostgreSQL container will run on the default port (5432).

## 8. Known Issues & Potential Pitfalls

*   **Database Migrations**: Drizzle doesn’t auto-generate migration SQL.\
    *Mitigation*: In v1, document how to manually sync schema or integrate `drizzle-kit` later.
*   **Env Var Management**: Missing or misnamed `.env` entries will break auth or DB connection.\
    *Mitigation*: Provide a robust `README.md` with a sample `.env.example` and clear instructions.
*   **Docker Networking**: If another service occupies port 5432, the Postgres container will fail.\
    *Mitigation*: Allow users to override ports via environment variables.
*   **Styling Conflicts**: Customizing shadcn/ui components without understanding Tailwind may lead to CSS specificity issues.\
    *Mitigation*: Include a brief style-override guide in documentation.

